  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_FLORA_HERBAL_FOLIO",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "Dry the herbs separately. Boil clean cloth for wounds. Mend the old sleeves before another journey. Keep both paths around the spiritual tree clear. The last line reads: a refuge remains a refuge because someone cares for it.",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_CAVE_SCOUT_NOTE",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "I marked the wide gallery to the east. Below it, the smaller passage winds around the stone mass and meets the gallery twice. We heard the chime in the western chamber before we saw what followed it. The turns hid us from its eyes. There is a braced chute near the ladder, but its peg faces deeper into the cave. I will leave another mark by the broken prop if we reach it.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_CHAPEL_RELIEF_ROSTER",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "First week: water in the east store, blankets and dressings in the southern sacristy, names of the dead beside the western graves. Later entries replace meal counts with hours spent beside the red stone. The last volunteer underlined: This was meant to be a shelter.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_CHAPEL_RITUAL_NOTE",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "We called the stone a miracle because we needed one. We moved it behind the altar and stopped opening the door to strangers. When the bell rang by itself, we thought we had been answered. The handprints on the altar were not made in prayer.",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_CHAPEL_FOREST_ROUTE",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "If the chapel is lost, leave through the broken west wall. An old cart track farther into the forest ends at a huge oak with knotted roots. Travelers spoke of another stone face there. This is a lead, not a surveyed map; do not mistake the tree for safety.",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_EXPEDITION_TRANSFER_NOTE",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "The transport order is crossed out. Below it: Three of us described the same red face after sleeping here. When we moved the specimen, the scratching began outside its new tent. Pavel is hurt; the alarm test drew the creature away until he stepped out from behind the canvas. Cancel collection of the sample. Send transport for the wounded. We are leaving the equipment.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
